00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,360
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

222
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:29,720
 But I don't know him.

223
00:12:29,720 --> 00:12:32,320
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

224
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:34,640
 I don't have a personal relationship with him.

225
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:37,600
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

226
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:41,080
 So we go back to verse 44.

227
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:42,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

228
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:45,520
 Where John said, a prophet has no honor in his hometown.

229
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:47,000
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

230
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:55,720
 It's actually very difficult for the Galileans to accept Jesus.

231
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:57,400
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

232
00:12:57,400 --> 00:13:01,080
 Think about it.

233
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:04,320
 Some of them probably watched Jesus grow up.

