248
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:50,160
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

249
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:56,200
 Something in my mind saying something is wrong.

250
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:57,880
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

251
00:13:57,880 --> 00:14:00,480
 How can that be?

252
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:01,480
 I taught you everything.

253
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:03,000
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

254
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:08,560
 But he actually has something new to teach me.

255
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:11,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

256
00:14:11,040 --> 00:14:13,720
 But it feels so weird.

257
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:15,600
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

258
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:18,080
 But I tell you, brothers and sisters,

259
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:20,400
 the Samaritans did not have that feeling.

260
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:21,960
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

261
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:27,640
 They did not require any really miracles.

262
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:29,640
 They believed Jesus based on his words.

263
00:14:29,640 --> 00:14:31,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

264
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:37,960
 In verse 42, this is what they said.

265
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:39,720
 "Jesus is the Savior of the world."

266
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:41,240
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

267
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:48,280
 See, brothers and sisters, these signs

268
00:14:48,280 --> 00:14:52,440
 were meant to validate Jesus' claim of being the Messiah.

269
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:53,840
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

270
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:59,320
 That he's the son of God so people

271
00:14:59,320 --> 00:15:00,600
 can put their trust in him.

272
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:01,920
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

273
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:06,240
 These signs were intended to inspire faith,

274
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:07,720
 not to please the people.

275
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:09,280
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

276
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:13,920
 There is no authentic relationship,

277
00:15:13,920 --> 00:15:16,080
 and the people don't have to make any commitments.

278
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:17,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

279
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:24,840
 These people's faith are shallow.

280
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

281
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:28,720
 They don't know Jesus personally.

282
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:29,920
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

283
00:15:29,920 --> 00:15:32,840
 They only want Jesus to perform for them.

284
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:34,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

285
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:37,760
 They don't even care who is Jesus,

286
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:42,320
 or they don't want any relationship.

287
00:15:42,320 --> 00:15:43,640
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

288
00:15:43,640 --> 00:15:48,440
 I can tell you, most people in Taiwan are like this.

289
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:49,640
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

290
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:54,040
 Most people come to church for different reasons.

291
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:55,400
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

292
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:59,480
 They don't see Jesus as Lord and Savior.

293
00:15:59,480 --> 00:16:00,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

294
00:16:00,760 --> 00:16:06,800
 They see Jesus as more like a healer or a genie.

295
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:08,160
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

296
00:16:08,160 --> 00:16:15,640
 I totally understand that feeling.

297
00:16:15,640 --> 00:16:17,600
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

298
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:19,360
 Because when I first came to church,

299
00:16:19,360 --> 00:16:20,760
 it has nothing to do with Jesus.

300
00:16:20,760 --> 00:16:22,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

301
00:16:22,040 --> 00:16:28,040
 I came to church because of basketball and meeting people.

302
00:16:28,040 --> 00:16:29,400
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

303
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:35,080
 Jesus is far from my mind.

304
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:36,440
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

305
00:16:36,440 --> 00:16:44,080
 If you take a look, certain people come for a lunch.

306
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:45,440
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

307
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:48,240
 Some people want to practice English.

308
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:49,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

309
00:16:50,840 --> 00:16:54,160
 But they tell me, don't talk to me about Jesus.

310
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:56,200
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

311
00:16:56,200 --> 00:16:57,480
 I said, OK.

312
00:16:57,480 --> 00:16:58,560
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

313
00:16:58,560 --> 00:17:01,560
 But I cannot not share Jesus.

314
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:03,080
 That is part of my life.

315
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:04,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

316
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:12,480
 Some people come for music and English lessons.

317
00:17:12,480 --> 00:17:13,800
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

318
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:20,280
 I did not want to make these lessons, actually.

319
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:22,280
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

320
00:17:22,280 --> 00:17:24,720
 But the parents said, if you have nothing academic or good

321
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:27,400
 to learn, then my kids are not coming to church.

322
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:28,640
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

323
00:17:28,640 --> 00:17:37,160
 That's why my wife had to teach ukulele,

324
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:38,320
 and I had to teach English.

325
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:39,600
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

326
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:45,760
 We had a chance to break down an altar.

327
00:17:45,760 --> 00:17:47,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

328
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:53,640
 But overall, sometimes, even when brothers and sisters

329
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:57,480
 become Christians, their life is not transformed.

330
00:17:57,480 --> 00:17:58,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

331
00:17:58,760 --> 00:18:10,080
 In their heart, they just transfer one idol to another.

332
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:11,360
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

333
00:18:11,360 --> 00:18:18,320
 Jesus became another idol for them.

334
00:18:18,320 --> 00:18:21,400
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

335
00:18:21,400 --> 00:18:23,480
 See, they only want the blessing,

336
00:18:23,480 --> 00:18:25,840
 but not the relationship, brothers and sisters.

337
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:27,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

338
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:34,600
 My question is, how about us?

339
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:36,880
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

340
00:18:36,880 --> 00:18:38,760
 Is this what we do also?

341
00:18:38,760 --> 00:18:41,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

342
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:44,560
 That's why I don't want us to be fans.

343
00:18:44,560 --> 00:18:47,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

344
00:18:47,760 --> 00:18:49,280
 I want us to be disciples.

345
00:18:49,280 --> 00:18:51,640
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

346
00:18:51,640 --> 00:18:54,480
 But how is a disciple different from being a fan?

347
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:57,520
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

348
00:18:57,520 --> 00:19:00,280
 Therefore, let's look at how real faith looks like,

349
00:19:00,280 --> 00:19:01,640
 which brings my second point.

350
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:03,600
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

351
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:08,760
 My second point is Atlantic faith.

352
00:19:08,760 --> 00:19:11,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

353
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:12,000
 Let's go on.

354
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:18,000
 In verse 49, unlike the crowd, the official is very desperate

355
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:19,120
 at this time.

356
00:19:19,120 --> 00:19:21,600
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

357
00:19:21,600 --> 00:19:32,200
 Think about ourself.

358
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:33,320
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

359
00:19:33,320 --> 00:19:35,240
 When are we closest to God?

360
00:19:35,240 --> 00:19:38,840
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

361
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:40,520
 During our peaceful time.

362
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:42,360
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

363
00:19:42,360 --> 00:19:43,880
 When everything is going well.

364
00:19:43,880 --> 00:19:45,880
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

365
00:19:45,880 --> 00:19:49,520
 I'm sorry to say, that's when we're always farthest from God.

366
00:19:49,520 --> 00:19:54,320
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

367
00:19:54,320 --> 00:19:56,720
 It is usually during trials.

368
00:19:56,720 --> 00:20:03,000
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

369
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:06,920
 In verse 50, if you see in other gospel stories,

370
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:08,120
 this is the outcome.

371
00:20:08,120 --> 00:20:10,440
 Usually, this is what happened in other gospel story.

372
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:17,680
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

373
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:20,480
 After enough pleading, usually Jesus

374
00:20:20,480 --> 00:20:23,920
 will heal or take care of that person's problem.

375
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:27,400
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

376
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:29,360
 But this time, Jesus did not do that.

377
00:20:29,360 --> 00:20:32,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

378
00:20:32,120 --> 00:20:34,880
 My speculation is this.

379
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:37,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

380
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:40,840
 Jesus did not want to please these fans.

381
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:45,320
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

382
00:20:45,320 --> 00:20:47,800
 Because they were looking for another show.

383
00:20:47,800 --> 00:20:50,360
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

384
00:20:50,360 --> 00:20:52,880
 And Jesus wanted to also force the official

385
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:56,120
 to choose if he's willing to trust in Jesus

386
00:20:56,120 --> 00:20:58,000
 without seeing a miracle.

387
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:08,320
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

388
00:21:08,320 --> 00:21:12,000
 It is not normal for people to do things that are illogical.

389
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:14,840
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

390
00:21:14,840 --> 00:21:15,840
 An example.

391
00:21:15,840 --> 00:21:17,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

392
00:21:17,760 --> 00:21:22,040
 In Taiwan, if the doctor tells a patient

393
00:21:22,040 --> 00:21:24,840
 to go home without medicine, that is a no-no.

394
00:21:24,840 --> 00:21:32,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

395
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:33,560
 Even if I have a common cold, there

396
00:21:33,560 --> 00:21:36,440
 will be five different types of medicine to bring home.

397
00:21:36,440 --> 00:21:41,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

398
00:21:41,080 --> 00:21:43,720
 It got to a point that people feel like,

399
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:46,920
 if there is no medicine, that means you're not effective.

400
00:21:46,920 --> 00:21:52,320
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

401
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:55,320
 See, brothers and sisters, I need something

402
00:21:55,320 --> 00:21:58,040
 to look at, to grasp onto.

403
00:21:58,040 --> 00:22:01,960
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

404
00:22:01,960 --> 00:22:05,040
 So if I were the official, I would have the same feeling.

405
00:22:05,040 --> 00:22:10,800
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

406
00:22:10,800 --> 00:22:14,480
 It also shifts the official's mindset, his mentality,

407
00:22:14,480 --> 00:22:16,880
 from thinking about a quick fix to his problem.

408
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:22,160
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

409
00:22:22,160 --> 00:22:25,560
 Think about when you're stressed out for your job,

410
00:22:25,560 --> 00:22:27,480
 for your family, or even your kids.

411
00:22:27,480 --> 00:22:30,200
 You want to fix the problem right away.

412
00:22:30,200 --> 00:22:41,240
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

413
00:22:41,240 --> 00:22:43,520
 You want Jesus to give you a pill,

414
00:22:43,520 --> 00:22:46,480
 and just swallow it, and fix the problem.

415
00:22:46,480 --> 00:22:51,640
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

416
00:22:51,640 --> 00:22:54,960
 But in this story, Jesus did not give the official a pill.

417
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:57,960
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

418
00:22:57,960 --> 00:23:01,960
 He gave the official his word, which is to go home.

419
00:23:01,960 --> 00:23:05,680
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

420
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:07,440
 See, with no other choice, the official

421
00:23:07,440 --> 00:23:10,360
 has to decide to believe in Jesus' word.

422
00:23:10,360 --> 00:23:14,240
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

423
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:17,920
 And this belief is a sign of true progression of faith.

424
00:23:17,920 --> 00:23:22,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

425
00:23:22,760 --> 00:23:26,840
 See, true faith is not just based on observed miracle,

426
00:23:26,840 --> 00:23:28,520
 but based on the word of God.

427
00:23:28,520 --> 00:23:35,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

428
00:23:35,040 --> 00:23:38,800
 And his action, by starting his journey home,

429
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:40,960
 shows that he's consistent with the faith.

430
00:23:40,960 --> 00:23:45,840
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

431
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:49,240
 See, in verse 51, as the official is almost home,

432
00:23:49,240 --> 00:23:51,240
 his servant came out to meet him with good news

433
00:23:51,240 --> 00:23:52,520
 that his son is alive.

434
00:23:52,520 --> 00:24:01,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

435
00:24:01,080 --> 00:24:05,160
 Assuming the official is happy, I

436
00:24:05,160 --> 00:24:07,720
 would think he would normally focus all his attention

437
00:24:07,720 --> 00:24:08,640
 on his son.

438
00:24:08,640 --> 00:24:15,160
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

439
00:24:15,160 --> 00:24:18,200
 He might want to see him and spend time with him.

440
00:24:18,200 --> 00:24:21,880
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

441
00:24:21,880 --> 00:24:24,800
 Or even find a doctor to see if he's truly well.

442
00:24:24,800 --> 00:24:27,840
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

443
00:24:27,840 --> 00:24:31,960
 Instead, he focuses his attention back to Jesus' word.

444
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:36,360
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

445
00:24:36,360 --> 00:24:37,080
 Sorry.

446
00:24:37,080 --> 00:24:39,720
 In 52, when asked about the time,

447
00:24:39,720 --> 00:24:42,600
 the servant said it was yesterday at 1 o'clock.

448
00:24:42,600 --> 00:24:44,480
 Yesterday at 1 PM.

449
00:24:44,480 --> 00:24:50,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

450
00:24:50,480 --> 00:24:53,480
 Based on this, the official spent a night traveling back

451
00:24:53,480 --> 00:24:55,040
 to his hometown.

452
00:24:55,040 --> 00:25:01,520
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

453
00:25:01,520 --> 00:25:03,200
 Think about it, brothers and sisters.

454
00:25:03,200 --> 00:25:06,840
 This night will be a very, very difficult night.

455
00:25:06,840 --> 00:25:10,320
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

456
00:25:10,320 --> 00:25:15,120
 He has to wrestle with the decision because he wasn't sure

457
00:25:15,120 --> 00:25:17,160
 what Jesus said would come true or not.

458
00:25:17,160 --> 00:25:23,720
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

459
00:25:23,720 --> 00:25:27,400
 But it is during this time, these struggles,

460
00:25:27,400 --> 00:25:29,440
 that God will strengthen us and help

461
00:25:29,440 --> 00:25:31,280
 us to put more trust in him.

462
00:25:31,280 --> 00:25:38,280
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

463
00:25:38,280 --> 00:25:40,480
 At last, he verified Jesus' word,

464
00:25:40,480 --> 00:25:42,280
 and it was proved to be true.

465
00:25:42,280 --> 00:25:46,640
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

466
00:25:46,640 --> 00:25:49,160
 In verse 53, unlike the crowd, he

467
00:25:49,160 --> 00:25:52,560
 was willing to make a real commitment to follow Jesus.

468
00:25:52,560 --> 00:26:04,600
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

469
00:26:04,600 --> 00:26:09,640
 The miracle helped push him through with his faith

470
00:26:09,640 --> 00:26:11,240
 in trusting in Jesus.

471
00:26:11,240 --> 00:26:16,440
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

472
00:26:16,440 --> 00:26:18,680
 He didn't just stop there.

473
00:26:18,680 --> 00:26:21,520
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

474
00:26:21,520 --> 00:26:26,920
 He also told the good news to his family.

475
00:26:26,920 --> 00:26:31,720
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

476
00:26:31,720 --> 00:26:34,720
 See, brothers and sisters, true faith is a progression,

477
00:26:34,720 --> 00:26:36,320
 and it's not a one-time deal.

478
00:26:36,320 --> 00:26:41,280
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

479
00:26:41,280 --> 00:26:45,360
 God will always give us trials in different seasons

480
00:26:45,360 --> 00:26:47,880
 of our life so we could put trust in him more.

481
00:26:47,880 --> 00:26:54,720
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

482
00:26:54,720 --> 00:26:57,440
 Throughout my three years, there are not many people

483
00:26:57,440 --> 00:26:58,760
 who's willing to do that.

484
00:26:58,760 --> 00:27:01,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

485
00:27:01,760 --> 00:27:04,480
 But because of time-wise, I only got two examples for you.

486
00:27:04,480 --> 00:27:08,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

487
00:27:08,760 --> 00:27:11,760
 First one is I have a group of brothers and sisters.

488
00:27:11,760 --> 00:27:14,040
 This is a Bible study that I host.

489
00:27:14,040 --> 00:27:19,800
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

490
00:27:19,800 --> 00:27:24,560
 And they asked to study the Bible like a year or two ago.

491
00:27:24,560 --> 00:27:30,360
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

492
00:27:30,360 --> 00:27:34,880
 And I told them, let's end the Bible study this January.

493
00:27:34,880 --> 00:27:41,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

494
00:27:41,040 --> 00:27:43,400
 Because I was about to end my time

495
00:27:43,400 --> 00:27:44,680
 with this church in February.

496
00:27:44,680 --> 00:27:47,920
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

497
00:27:47,920 --> 00:27:51,600
 And February is Chinese New Year.

498
00:27:51,600 --> 00:27:53,840
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

499
00:27:53,840 --> 00:27:56,400
 And I thought they would have a lot of stuff to take care of.

500
00:27:56,400 --> 00:27:59,920
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

501
00:27:59,920 --> 00:28:02,880
 They said, Steve, Chinese New Year is different from before.

502
00:28:02,880 --> 00:28:04,400
 We don't take care of stuff anymore.

503
00:28:04,400 --> 00:28:05,360
 We just go out to eat.

504
00:28:05,360 --> 00:28:12,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

505
00:28:12,760 --> 00:28:15,800
 They said, since you're here for another month,

506
00:28:15,800 --> 00:28:17,200
 we want to do more Bible study.

507
00:28:17,200 --> 00:28:20,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

508
00:28:20,080 --> 00:28:24,040
 You know, that's the most happiest thing for my job.

509
00:28:24,040 --> 00:28:26,120
 I really enjoy doing that as a missionary.

510
00:28:26,120 --> 00:28:33,960
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

511
00:28:33,960 --> 00:28:35,960
 Another is a family.

512
00:28:35,960 --> 00:28:38,200
 The girl's name is Lucy.

513
00:28:38,200 --> 00:28:41,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

514
00:28:41,040 --> 00:28:45,680
 This family came to our church through our summer camp,

515
00:28:45,680 --> 00:28:47,280
 our VBS camp.

516
00:28:47,280 --> 00:28:52,280
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

517
00:28:52,280 --> 00:28:54,040
 They were very poor.

518
00:28:54,040 --> 00:28:56,520
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

519
00:28:56,520 --> 00:28:59,520
 Because they spent all their money on their health.

520
00:28:59,520 --> 00:29:06,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

521
00:29:06,760 --> 00:29:10,000
 And this is not the first church they came to.

522
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:13,320
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

523
00:29:13,320 --> 00:29:15,760
 After a while, when we get to know each other a little bit

524
00:29:15,760 --> 00:29:21,200
 more, she told me this story, the mom.

525
00:29:21,200 --> 00:29:23,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

526
00:29:23,040 --> 00:29:30,760
 Is that at one of my church, the minister said this to me.

527
00:29:30,760 --> 00:29:33,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

528
00:29:33,040 --> 00:29:35,200
 Do you know why you and your whole family is sick?

529
00:29:35,200 --> 00:29:37,000
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

530
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:38,720
 Because you don't believe in Jesus.

531
00:29:38,720 --> 00:29:40,280
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

532
00:29:40,280 --> 00:29:42,400
 Man, that really hurt me, you know that?

533
00:29:42,400 --> 00:29:46,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

534
00:29:46,120 --> 00:29:48,640
 Because that's not the true gospel.

535
00:29:48,640 --> 00:29:52,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

536
00:29:52,120 --> 00:29:56,800
 And it got to a point that Lucy, the girl,

537
00:29:56,800 --> 00:30:01,080
 was eating congee for the whole month.

538
00:30:01,080 --> 00:30:05,840
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

539
00:30:05,840 --> 00:30:07,320
 And they were asking us, is there

540
00:30:07,320 --> 00:30:10,480
 any stuff that you have in the church refrigerator?

541
00:30:10,480 --> 00:30:11,440
 Can we take them?

542
00:30:11,440 --> 00:30:16,840
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

543
00:30:16,840 --> 00:30:18,360
 I said, take everything you want.

544
00:30:18,360 --> 00:30:21,200
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

545
00:30:21,200 --> 00:30:23,040
 And then we went home, different ways.

546
00:30:23,040 --> 00:30:24,400
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

547
00:30:24,400 --> 00:30:26,920
 But that night during dinner, I was really hot.

548
00:30:26,920 --> 00:30:28,160
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

549
00:30:28,160 --> 00:30:29,360
 I was really mad.

550
00:30:29,360 --> 00:30:31,600
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

551
00:30:31,600 --> 00:30:35,680
 And I was mad during eating hot pot.

552
00:30:35,680 --> 00:30:39,360
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

553
00:30:39,360 --> 00:30:40,680
 So I was extra hot.

554
00:30:40,680 --> 00:30:43,640
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

555
00:30:43,640 --> 00:30:46,760
 My mind was, I want to find this minister and beat him up.

556
00:30:46,760 --> 00:30:51,360
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

557
00:30:51,360 --> 00:30:53,480
 But another thought came to me.

558
00:30:53,480 --> 00:30:57,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

559
00:30:57,120 --> 00:31:00,120
 I told my wife and my family, we are going to the supermarket

560
00:31:00,120 --> 00:31:00,880
 right now.

561
00:31:00,880 --> 00:31:05,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

562
00:31:05,480 --> 00:31:07,640
 We are going to load up the cart with grocery,

563
00:31:07,640 --> 00:31:09,480
 and we're going to bring it to their house.

564
00:31:09,480 --> 00:31:13,360
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

565
00:31:13,360 --> 00:31:15,240
 And we told him, this is from the church.

566
00:31:15,240 --> 00:31:16,560
 This is from Jesus.

567
00:31:16,560 --> 00:31:17,600
 This is unconditional.

568
00:31:17,600 --> 00:31:25,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

569
00:31:25,080 --> 00:31:26,720
 After a couple of weeks--

570
00:31:26,720 --> 00:31:29,520
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

571
00:31:29,520 --> 00:31:33,880
 She was willing to ask, Steve Shirley, what is the gospel?

572
00:31:33,880 --> 00:31:41,160
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

573
00:31:41,160 --> 00:31:46,600
 I feel like they're willing to ask this question.

574
00:31:46,600 --> 00:31:50,080
 Is this that they saw a difference in our lives?

575
00:31:50,080 --> 00:31:54,720
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

576
00:31:54,720 --> 00:31:58,600
 But brothers and sisters, I want to know, how do you see Jesus?

577
00:31:58,600 --> 00:32:02,800
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

578
00:32:02,800 --> 00:32:05,800
 Is he a celebrity, or he's your Lord?

579
00:32:05,800 --> 00:32:09,880
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

580
00:32:09,880 --> 00:32:14,360
 If Jesus is your Lord, does your life matches the gospel?

581
00:32:14,360 --> 00:32:19,920
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

582
00:32:19,920 --> 00:32:22,400
 You see, missions is an integrated part

583
00:32:22,400 --> 00:32:23,760
 of our Christian life.

584
00:32:23,760 --> 00:32:27,960
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

585
00:32:27,960 --> 00:32:31,480
 You are a missionary in your sphere of influence.

586
00:32:31,480 --> 00:32:36,400
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

587
00:32:36,400 --> 00:32:38,840
 See, the only difference between me and you guys

588
00:32:38,840 --> 00:32:40,600
 is that we serve in a different place.

589
00:32:40,600 --> 00:32:44,880
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

590
00:32:44,880 --> 00:32:46,520
 Remember the Great Commission?

591
00:32:46,520 --> 00:32:49,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

592
00:32:49,080 --> 00:32:50,600
 Basically, it's to go to all nations

593
00:32:50,600 --> 00:32:53,240
 and proclaim the gospel, right?

594
00:32:53,240 --> 00:32:57,560
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

595
00:32:57,560 --> 00:33:00,240
 But some of us might be saying, I don't know enough.

596
00:33:00,240 --> 00:33:01,960
 I'm not capable of doing that.

597
00:33:01,960 --> 00:33:05,600
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

598
00:33:05,600 --> 00:33:08,200
 I can tell you, I have the same feeling.

599
00:33:08,200 --> 00:33:10,920
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

600
00:33:10,920 --> 00:33:12,760
 I don't really have much talents.

601
00:33:12,760 --> 00:33:15,680
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

602
00:33:15,680 --> 00:33:18,000
 I don't know a lick of music.

603
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:21,680
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

604
00:33:21,680 --> 00:33:23,520
 I'm not a good speaker, actually.

605
00:33:23,520 --> 00:33:26,160
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

606
00:33:26,160 --> 00:33:29,720
 I don't have really much skills to teach kids.

607
00:33:29,720 --> 00:33:33,840
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

608
00:33:33,840 --> 00:33:35,800
 But I want you to know, God don't

609
00:33:35,800 --> 00:33:38,560
 use those who are talented a lot of times.

610
00:33:38,560 --> 00:33:44,440
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

611
00:33:44,440 --> 00:33:47,200
 God use those who say they are available.

612
00:33:47,200 --> 00:33:53,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

613
00:33:53,120 --> 00:33:56,560
 Because God will supply you with the resource

614
00:33:56,560 --> 00:33:57,960
 to get the job done.

615
00:33:57,960 --> 00:34:02,200
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

616
00:34:02,200 --> 00:34:03,680
 My thing is that in your company,

617
00:34:03,680 --> 00:34:05,960
 don't your company supply you with the basic resource

618
00:34:05,960 --> 00:34:07,480
 to get to do your job?

619
00:34:07,480 --> 00:34:13,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

620
00:34:13,120 --> 00:34:15,920
 But one thing I don't want you, besides the Greek mission,

621
00:34:15,920 --> 00:34:18,920
 I don't want you to forget about one other thing.

622
00:34:18,920 --> 00:34:28,440
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

623
00:34:28,440 --> 00:34:30,640
 Which is the great commandment.

624
00:34:30,640 --> 00:34:35,000
 Which is to love God with all your heart, soul, mind,

625
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:36,280
 and strength, right?

626
00:34:36,280 --> 00:34:37,820
 But the second one is to love people

627
00:34:37,820 --> 00:34:39,280
 like you would love yourself.

628
00:34:39,280 --> 00:34:46,240
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

629
00:34:46,240 --> 00:34:49,900
 Don't preach the gospel like you're giving a sales pitch.

630
00:34:49,900 --> 00:34:55,240
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

631
00:34:55,240 --> 00:34:56,960
 Love that person.

632
00:34:56,960 --> 00:35:02,840
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

633
00:35:02,840 --> 00:35:05,120
 What's going to happen in the next four years, brothers

634
00:35:05,120 --> 00:35:06,200
 and sisters?

635
00:35:06,200 --> 00:35:09,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

636
00:35:09,080 --> 00:35:10,920
 I will be moving to a new church.

637
00:35:10,920 --> 00:35:13,680
 We are going to-- oops.

638
00:35:13,680 --> 00:35:16,040
 I live in Kaohsiung, but we're going to move a little bit

639
00:35:16,040 --> 00:35:17,460
 to Chiayi.

640
00:35:17,460 --> 00:35:23,280
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

641
00:35:23,280 --> 00:35:24,600
 So this is our church.

642
00:35:24,600 --> 00:35:26,120
 It's called a grace place.

643
00:35:26,120 --> 00:35:29,720
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

644
00:35:29,720 --> 00:35:32,640
 It's an even more rural area than where I was before.

645
00:35:32,640 --> 00:35:43,200
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

646
00:35:43,200 --> 00:35:46,360
 This is some of the things I will be doing.

647
00:35:46,360 --> 00:35:49,600
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

648
00:35:49,600 --> 00:35:51,040
 You pastor again.

649
00:35:51,040 --> 00:35:53,240
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

650
00:35:53,240 --> 00:35:55,440
 Yeah, and that's something I really enjoy doing.

651
00:35:55,440 --> 00:35:58,280
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

652
00:35:58,280 --> 00:35:59,600
 And I could do this every day.

653
00:35:59,600 --> 00:36:01,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

654
00:36:01,480 --> 00:36:03,920
 Yeah, but God continue to allow me with the energy.

655
00:36:03,920 --> 00:36:08,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

656
00:36:08,040 --> 00:36:10,560
 But this is the church that we will be in.

657
00:36:10,560 --> 00:36:13,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

658
00:36:13,120 --> 00:36:16,480
 Another small church, about 30 to 40 people.

659
00:36:16,480 --> 00:36:19,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

660
00:36:19,480 --> 00:36:21,960
 Typical church in Taiwan, that's how big it is.

661
00:36:21,960 --> 00:36:26,320
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

662
00:36:26,320 --> 00:36:29,040
 Again, I'm going there to learn how to be a better pastor.

663
00:36:29,040 --> 00:36:34,520
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

664
00:36:34,520 --> 00:36:36,120
 Yeah, that's one thing is that I need

665
00:36:36,120 --> 00:36:37,840
 to practice my Chinese, Mandarin.

666
00:36:37,840 --> 00:36:41,000
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

667
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:43,240
 I feel comfortable speaking to you in Mandarin

668
00:36:43,240 --> 00:36:45,680
 when we're just having a dialogue, an informal dialogue.

669
00:36:45,680 --> 00:36:52,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

670
00:36:52,080 --> 00:36:54,520
 But formal speaking is another level.

671
00:36:54,520 --> 00:36:58,000
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

672
00:36:58,000 --> 00:37:00,560
 But I don't want to hide in my comfort zone.

673
00:37:00,560 --> 00:37:03,920
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

674
00:37:03,920 --> 00:37:05,960
 I want to be able to tell the Taiwanese people

675
00:37:05,960 --> 00:37:08,280
 the gospel in their native language.

676
00:37:08,280 --> 00:37:14,920
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

677
00:37:14,920 --> 00:37:17,840
 This is what I did for 15 minutes,

678
00:37:17,840 --> 00:37:22,080
 telling my testimony in Mandarin.

679
00:37:22,080 --> 00:37:27,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

680
00:37:27,760 --> 00:37:29,400
 The Mandarin is really bad.

681
00:37:29,400 --> 00:37:31,400
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

682
00:37:31,400 --> 00:37:33,640
 But my mentality is I don't care.

683
00:37:33,640 --> 00:37:35,720
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

684
00:37:35,720 --> 00:37:37,040
 I need to keep practicing.

685
00:37:37,040 --> 00:37:39,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

686
00:37:39,760 --> 00:37:41,400
 I need to keep messing up.

687
00:37:41,400 --> 00:37:43,880
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

688
00:37:43,880 --> 00:37:45,640
 That's the way how I will improve.

689
00:37:45,640 --> 00:37:47,920
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

690
00:37:47,920 --> 00:37:50,840
 Because I need to tell the people about the gospel

691
00:37:50,840 --> 00:37:52,080
 in the native language.

692
00:37:52,080 --> 00:37:57,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

693
00:37:57,080 --> 00:37:58,840
 Thank you, brothers and sisters.

694
00:37:58,840 --> 00:38:00,720
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

695
00:38:00,720 --> 00:38:01,240
 Thank you.

696
00:38:01,240 --> 00:38:02,120
 This is my sharing.

697
00:38:02,120 --> 00:38:04,280
 And I thank you for always praying for us

698
00:38:04,280 --> 00:38:05,560
 as we are in the mission field.

699
00:38:05,560 --> 00:38:08,600
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

